{"name":"On Thin Ice","hex":"#d1e8f1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"on thin ice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["In a dangerous, hazardous, or delicate situation; at risk."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Dangerously, hazardously, delicately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/on_thin_ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"On Thin Ice (comedy group)","blocks":[{"text":"On Thin Ice (OTI) is Harvard College's oldest improvisational comedy group. OTI specializes in short-form improvisational theater taking the form of various comedy games in the style of Whose Line Is It Anyway?."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/OTI_Performing.jpg/330px-OTI_Performing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_Thin_Ice_(comedy_group)","wikidata":"Q16254617"},{"title":"On Thin Ice (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"On Thin Ice is a documentary following a team of three consisting of Ben Fogle, James Cracknell, and Ed Coats in their race across Antarctica to the South Pole. The series covers the whole experience, beginning with training efforts in Switzerland and vigorous exercises elsewhere. The team began their race to the South Pole shortly after New Year's Day 2009. The series also covers the various calamities experienced by Ben Fogle, who only a short while before the trip had contracted a highly dangerous tropical skin-eating disease."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_Thin_Ice_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q7091161"},{"title":"On Thin Ice (1925 film)","blocks":[{"text":"On Thin Ice is a 1925 American silent crime drama film directed by Mal St. Clair and starring Tom Moore, Edith Roberts, and William Russell. It was produced and distributed by Warner Bros. and based upon a 1924 novel by Alice Ross Colver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/On_Thin_Ice_%28SAYRE_14567%29.jpg/330px-On_Thin_Ice_%28SAYRE_14567%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_Thin_Ice_(1925_film)","wikidata":"Q30602089"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/OTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg/500px-OTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/OTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg/1280px-OTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/OTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg/500px-OTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"On Thin Ice sings the final note of a musical improv scene at the Hasty Pudding's annual Fall Show. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOTIPuddingPerfomance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Ice_Ih_Crystal_Lattice.png/500px-Ice_Ih_Crystal_Lattice.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, 